    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0907" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4261: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-12-16T12:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">December 16,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 2:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>240. … Chamorro turned over army yesterday, left Managua this morning at 4
                    o’clock, arrived at Corinto at 10 whence he is to sail today or tomorrow on a
                    diplomatic mission to principal European countries.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d519-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d519-f1" n="39" xml:id="d519-f1-content">
                <p>General Chamorro sailed from Corinto on December 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
